    "text": "To determine the number of unused hats, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of hats initially brought home.\n2. Subtract the number of hats that were torn off.\n3. Subtract the number of hats that were used during the party.\n4. The result will be the number of unused hats.\n\nLet's go through each step in detail:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of hats initially brought home:\n   \\[\n   3 \\text{ bags} \\times 15 \\text{ hats per bag} = 45 \\text{ hats}\n   \\]\n\n2. Subtract the number of hats that were torn off:\n   \\[\n   45 \\text{ hats} - 5 \\text{ hats} = 40 \\text{ hats}\n   \\]\n\n3. Subtract the number of hats that were used during the party:\n   \\[\n   40 \\text{ hats} - 25 \\text{ hats} = 15 \\text{ hats}\n   \\]\n\nSo, the number of unused hats is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).",
